## Frontend-to-backend type mapping

The backend producer is:

- tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/AsrsG2PApplicationDef.java
- tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/asrs.kt
- tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/data.kt

The display envelope is created as DisplayWidgets. Each JSON-backed entry is created through ApplicationDef.getData(name, data), which serializes the payload as a DisplayRawData widget. The frontend then locates the widget by name and parses widget.data.

~~~text
AsrsG2PApplicationDef.displayState()
  -> DisplayWidgets
  -> DisplayRawData(name, JSON(data))
  -> RuntimeStore.deviceState.displayState.displayData.widgets
  -> AsrsWorkstationStore getter
  -> Vue component
~~~

### RAW_DATA mapping

#### ports

Frontend:

- widget name: ports
- getter: AsrsWorkstationStore.ports
- consumer: PortsViewer
- frontend item type: port object with name, state, taskGroup, taskCount

Backend:

~~~text
PortData
  package: com.onomatic.tes.activity.g2p.application
  source: tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/asrs.kt
~~~

~~~ts
PortData {
  name: string,
  tote: string,
  selected: boolean,
  taskGroup: string,
  state: CarouselState,
  taskCount: Long
}
~~~

Backend construction:

~~~text
AsrsG2PApplicationDef.getPorts(session)
  -> session.getPorts()
  -> new PortData(...)
  -> getData("ports", getPorts(session))
~~~

Important differences:

- Backend also sends tote and selected, but the current PortsViewer does not use them.
- Backend taskCount is Long; JSON is consumed as a JavaScript number.
- Backend state is CarouselState; the frontend compares/display-uses its serialized value, including MOVING.
- The current backend code explicitly sets selected to false.

#### tote

Frontend:

- widget name: tote
- getter: AsrsWorkstationStore.tote
- consumers: ToteViewer and the store shelf getter
- frontend type: IToteState

Backend:

~~~text
ToteData
ToteBinData
SelectedToteBinData
  package: com.onomatic.tes.activity.g2p.application
  source: tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/asrs.kt
~~~

~~~ts
ToteData {
  referenceNo: string,
  name: string,
  layout: Layout | null,
  bins: ToteBinData[],
  selectedBin: SelectedToteBinData | null
}

ToteBinData {
  referenceNo: string,
  name: string,
  layout: Layout | null
}

SelectedToteBinData {
  name: string,
  quantity: ItemQuantity
}
~~~

Backend construction:

~~~text
AsrsG2PApplicationDef.getTote(session)
  -> session.getTote()
  -> LocationRepository lookup
  -> PositionRepository.findAllByLocation(...)
  -> ToteBinData(...)
  -> SelectedToteBinData(task position, task quantity)
  -> ToteData(...)
  -> getData("tote", getTote(session))
~~~

Important differences:

- The backend ToteData has referenceNo and layout; the frontend IToteState currently declares only name, bins, and selectedBin.
- Backend bin layout is a Layout object; the frontend ToteViewer currently does not use it.
- selectedBin is nullable on the backend, but ToteViewer accesses store.tote.selectedBin.name when a tote is rendered. An active task therefore needs a selected bin.
- ItemQuantity supplies the selected-bin quantity and unit. The current frontend displays the quantity with a hardcoded EA suffix.

#### workstation

Frontend:

- widget name: workstation
- getters: mode, paused, assignable, suspendable, canPauseTasks
- consumers: page toolbar and assignment controls
- frontend type: inferred object parsed by AsrsWorkstationStore

Backend:

~~~text
WorkstationData
  package: com.onomatic.tes.activity.g2p.application
  source: tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/data.kt
~~~

~~~ts
WorkstationData {
  activity: G2PActivityType,
  taskAssignmentMode: TaskAssignmentMode,
  hasPausedTasks: boolean,
  canPauseTasks: boolean
}
~~~

Backend construction:

~~~text
AsrsG2PApplicationDef.getWorkstation(session)
  -> new WorkstationData(
       session.getCurrentActivity(),
       session.getTaskAssignmentMode(),
       false,
       false
     )
  -> getData("workstation", getWorkstation(session))
~~~

Important differences:

- Frontend mode expects serialized activity values such as pick/order and putaway/container.
- Frontend checks taskAssignmentMode against the string NONE; backend type is TaskAssignmentMode.
- The current producer passes false for hasPausedTasks and canPauseTasks in this deprecated displayState path, so the corresponding toolbar controls may remain disabled unless a newer producer populates them.

#### staging

Frontend:

- widget name: staging
- getter: AsrsWorkstationStore.stations
- consumers: PutwallViewer, PutwallCard, assignment dialogs, ShortPickDialog
- frontend type: IStationState[]

Backend:

~~~text
StagingStationData
  package: com.onomatic.tes.activity.g2p.application
  source: tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/data.kt
~~~

~~~ts
StagingStationData {
  id: UUID,
  name: string,
  taskCount: Long,
  taskId: ActivityTaskItemId | null,
  orderNo: string,
  container: string,
  instructions: string,
  quantity: BigDecimal,
  unit: string
}
~~~

Backend construction:

~~~text
AsrsG2PApplicationDef.getStagingStations(session)
  -> session.getStagingAreas()
  -> activity-specific pick/putaway task lookup
  -> new StagingStationData(...)
  -> getData("staging", getStagingStations(session))
~~~

Frontend mapping:

~~~ts
IStationState {
  name: string,
  taskCount?: number,
  orderNo?: string,
  container?: string,
  instructions?: string,
  quantity?: string,
  unit?: string,
  taskId?: any
}
~~~

Important differences:

- Backend id is present but the frontend IStationState does not declare it.
- Backend taskId is ActivityTaskItemId; the frontend treats it as any and later sends it as the task identifier for short-pick.
- Backend quantity is BigDecimal; JSON becomes a numeric value or serialized numeric value depending on the mapper.
- Backend instructions currently return the literal string "null" from extractInstructions().
- For putaway, the backend intentionally fills both orderNo and container with the task reference number because the UI primarily reads orderNo.

### DisplayFields mapping

The following entries are not produced by asrs.kt. They are DisplayFields widgets created by AsrsG2PApplicationDef.getCurrentTaskFields(...).

Backend producer:

~~~text
AsrsG2PApplicationDef.getCurrentTaskFields(HandleItemPositionDef)
  -> DisplayFields("item")
  -> DisplayFields("task")
  -> DisplayFields("position")
~~~

#### item

Backend widget: DisplayFields named item.

Created fields:

~~~text
itemName       -> STRING -> item master name
vendorNo       -> STRING -> item master vendor property
manufacturerNo -> STRING -> item master manufacturer property
imageURL       -> IMAGE  -> item master image URL property
~~~

Frontend behavior:

- Uses every item element except imageURL as DisplayFieldSet fields.
- Uses imageURL for the product image.
- Does not currently distinguish backend DisplayDataType values in the field renderer.

#### task

Backend widget: DisplayFields named task.

Created fields:

~~~text
itemNo   -> STRING   -> current task item number
quantity -> QUANTITY -> current task ItemQuantity
~~~

Frontend behavior:

- Reads task.itemNo as the displayed item name.
- Reads task.quantity.quantity for the summary quantity.
- Hardcodes the displayed unit to EA.

#### position

Backend widget: DisplayFields named position.

Created fields:

~~~text
position  -> STRING -> position reference number
carousel  -> STRING -> parent carousel name
carrier   -> STRING -> carrier/location parent name
shelf     -> STRING -> shelf/location name
bin       -> STRING -> first two characters of position name
binDepth  -> STRING -> last two characters of position name
~~~

Frontend behavior:

- Converts widget.elements into an object through AsrsWorkstationStore.position.
- Uses the presence of this widget to distinguish standing from waiting.
- The detailed position display in AsrsProcessSection is currently commented out.

### Backend display infrastructure

The common backend types are:

~~~text
DisplayWidgets
DisplayRawData
DisplayFields
DisplayField
DisplayDataType
~~~

Relevant source areas:

- tes-coreapi/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/device/application/model.kt
- tes-engine/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/engine/core/model/application/ApplicationDef.java

DisplayRawData contains:

~~~ts
{
  name: string,
  data: string | null
}
~~~

The data field is the JSON serialization of PortData, ToteData, WorkstationData, StagingStationData, or another backend payload.

### Additional backend types

The payloads above reference these domain types:

- CarouselState for port state.
- G2PActivityType for workstation activity.
- TaskAssignmentMode for workstation assignment mode.
- Layout for tote/carrier layout metadata.
- ItemQuantity for selected-bin and task quantities.
- ItemQuantityInfo for carrier selected-bin quantities.
- ActivityTaskItemId for staging task identifiers.
- BigDecimal for staging quantities.
- UUID for staging station identifiers.

### Current producer caveat

The observed producer methods in AsrsG2PApplicationDef are marked Deprecated:

- displayState
- getWorkstation
- getTote
- getPorts
- getStagingStations
- getCurrentTaskFields

This mapping documents the payload contract used by the current ASRS UI and the legacy/deprecated producer path. If a newer state producer replaces these methods, verify widget names and serialized field shapes again.
